            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hello @necronyxon,\n\nThanks for the issue!\n\nI don't think that the local session of the previous path being in the 'detected' list is a bug. I replayed the steps you provided using [minimax](https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax).\n\nAfter step 5, having selected the global session for the other path, the \"now previous\" local session is indeed still present in the list. However, as I am now in another path, it is not provided by `lua require(\"mini.sessions\").select()` anymore. Also, if the \"now current\" path has a local Session.vim of its own, that will be included by `select`.\n\n ~~Closing as \"as expected\"~~.",
