            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> ... However, the documentation specifies that \"read\" updates the session list. Reopening...\n\nYeah, *technically* not adhering to the documentation is a bad thing. So either documentation needs to be updated or the code. I think extra re-detecting after reading a session but before execute hook is okay here (one extra `H.detect_sessions()` call).\n\n@abeldekat, would you be up to fixing this? The code is one line plus comment, but testing might be not trivial.\n\n---\n\nNote to future self. All problems would be gone if instead of exporting a `MiniSessions.detected` array there is a `MiniSessions.get()` that re-detects and returns the same data. It is a breaking change, so would probably require some strong use case.",
